COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[124,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nIdentify some reprehensible acts and convey the rule of Allah on them, so that you will be absolved of responsibility.\nShare a message in which you explain that Allah likes an inquiry intended for action, and that He hates an inquiry for defiance and pretension.\nShare a message in which you warn others against prohibiting the lawful and permitting the unlawful.\nguid\nHaving a little of what Allah made lawful is better and more useful than having abundance of the harmful unlawful.\nEvil wealth does not benefit its owner, rather it harms him in his faith and life.\nDo not ask a scholar questions about pointless matters.\nrefl\nٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٩٨\nAllah made mercy an attribute reflected in His Holy Names, but He made the punishment an action of His, not included in His Holy Names. Ibn Taimyah: 2/561.\nThe verse induces fear and hope. Explain.\nٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٩٨\nMeaning: Let these contrasting attributes be in your hearts with certainty and conviction, knowing that He is severe in punishment, both in this world and in the Hereafter, to those who disobey Him, and that He is all-Forgiving and Merciful toward those who repent and obey Him. This knowledge will instill in your heart fear of His punishment and hope for His forgiveness and reward, thus you will conduct yourself in the light of these two principles, fear and hope. Al-Saadi: 245.\nWhat benefit is gained from knowing that Allah is severe in penalty and that He is Forgiving and Merciful?\nمَّا عَلَى ٱلرَّسُولِ إِلَّا ٱلۡبَلَٰغُۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَعۡلَمُ مَا تُبۡدُونَ وَمَا تَكۡتُمُونَ ٩٩\n(The Messenger's duty is only to convey the message), except for conveying the message, the Messenger does not control guidance, success nor recompense. Al-Qurtubi: 8/225.\nWhat is the duty of one who calls others to the path of Allah?\nقُل لَّا يَسۡتَوِي ٱلۡخَبِيثُ وَٱلطَّيِّبُ وَلَوۡ أَعۡجَبَكَ كَثۡرَةُ ٱلۡخَبِيثِۚ فَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ١٠٠\nEvil does not equate good in value, expenditure, status nor direction. Good sets to the right while evil sets to the left. Good leads to Paradise while evil leads to Hellfire. Al-Qurtubi: 8/226.\nExplain why evil does not equate good?\nقُل لَّا يَسۡتَوِي ٱلۡخَبِيثُ وَٱلطَّيِّبُ وَلَوۡ أَعۡجَبَكَ كَثۡرَةُ ٱلۡخَبِيثِۚ فَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ١٠٠\nTo Allah, the disbelievers and the believers are not equal, even if there is an abundance of disbelievers to the point of making one impressed by them. Even when the faithful ones are fewer in number, they are, in fact, the real winners of Allah's reward on the Day of Resurrection. The disbelievers, on the other hand, are the losers even though they are abundant in numbers. One should not be impressed by the abundant number of people who disobey Allah while He gives them respite and does not rush to punish them because eventually the eternal bliss is for the faithful. Al-Tabari: 11/96.\nA wise person is not impressed with the abundance of disbelievers. Explain in light of this verse.\nقُل لَّا يَسۡتَوِي ٱلۡخَبِيثُ وَٱلطَّيِّبُ وَلَوۡ أَعۡجَبَكَ كَثۡرَةُ ٱلۡخَبِيثِۚ فَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ١٠٠\n(Even if the abundance of evil may impress you) for it is of no benefit to the one who possesses it; rather, it is harmful in both spiritual and worldly terms. (So fear Allah, O people of understanding, so that you may be successful) here, Allah issues a command to men of understanding - that is, people of mature thinking and wisdom. They are addressed here because they are the ones to whom attention is paid, and it is hoped that there is good in them. Then, Allah makes clear that prosperity depends on fearing Him, which means complying with His commands and prohibitions. Whoever fears Allah will prosper, but whoever does not will incur loss and miss out on gains. Al-Saadi: 245.\nOnly the people of understanding are addressed in this verse. Why?\nقَدۡ سَأَلَهَا قَوۡمٞ مِّن قَبۡلِكُمۡ ثُمَّ أَصۡبَحُواْ بِهَا كَٰفِرِينَ ١٠٢\nThey asked about these things not to gain guidance, but only to mock and defy. Ibn Kathir: 2/100.\nWhat is the difference between a good question and a bad one?\nwords\nوَلِلسَّيَّارَةِFor the travelers\nوَالقَلاَئِدَGarlands by which sacrificial animals are identified\nبَحِيرَةٍA she-camel whose ear is cut and left for the sake of the idols after giving birth for the fifth time\nسَائِبَةٍA camel, a cow or ewe that is let loose for free pasture to fulfill a vow to the false gods"],[125,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nForbid something that is wrong today, with an effective manner and nice words, so that you may be among those whom Allah halts His punishment of the people on earth because of them.\nWrite your will before going to sleep tonight.\nAdvise those around you of the importance of writing a will.\nguid\nNeglecting what Allah Has revealed, and following the false ways of the forefathers and society are major causes for people's alienation from their faith and life.\nFollowing customs and traditions is commended if they do not contradict Sharia.\nIf the believers enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, then they are not harmed when others go astray.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ عَلَيۡكُمۡ أَنفُسَكُمۡۖ لَا يَضُرُّكُم مَّن ضَلَّ إِذَا ٱهۡتَدَيۡتُمۡۚ\nThis does not mean that neglecting to enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong will not harm the Muslim; in fact, his guidance cannot be complete unless he does what he is obliged to do of enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong. However, if he is unable to denounce evil by taking action and speaking out, but resents it in his heart, then those who have gone astray will not harm him. Al-Saadi: 246.\nHow do you respond to one who infers from this verse that enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong is not obligatory?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ عَلَيۡكُمۡ أَنفُسَكُمۡۖ لَا يَضُرُّكُم مَّن ضَلَّ إِذَا ٱهۡتَدَيۡتُمۡۚ\nAn ignorant person may misconstrue the apparent meaning of this verse that enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong as not obligatory; however, this verse indicates that an individual is relieved only after he carries out his duty but to no avail, as Allah says, (As long as you are guided) and no guidance is achieved when neglecting enjoining what is right. Al-Shanqiti: 1/459.\nWhen does the harm of misguidance affect its owner only?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ شَهَٰدَةُ بَيۡنِكُمۡ إِذَا حَضَرَ أَحَدَكُمُ ٱلۡمَوۡتُ حِينَ ٱلۡوَصِيَّةِ\nThe will is considered as valid, even if the individual reached the point where he was about to die, so long as he was still thinking clearly. Al-Saadi: 247.\nIs it acceptable for one who is about to die to make a will?\nفَأَصَٰبَتۡكُم مُّصِيبَةُ ٱلۡمَوۡتِۚ\nIn this verse, Allah has calls death a disaster. Even though death is a great disaster and a major calamity, but what is even a greater disaster is being heedless about it, turning away from its remembrance, neglecting to reflect on it and not working for what comes afterward. Indeed, death is a great lesson and an admonition to those who think. Al-Qurtubi: 8/264.\nIs death a disaster? What is even a greater disaster than death?\nتَحۡبِسُونَهُمَا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ فَيُقۡسِمَانِ بِٱللَّهِ\nDetaining witnesses after the prayer is to indicate the importance of the time of the prayer, and as a deterrence since it is witnessed by the angels. Al-Qurtubi: 8/266.\nTaking the oath is prescribed after the prayer. Why?\nفَيُقۡسِمَانِ بِٱللَّهِ إِنِ ٱرۡتَبۡتُمۡ لَا نَشۡتَرِي بِهِۦ ثَمَنٗا وَلَوۡ كَانَ ذَا قُرۡبَىٰ وَلَا نَكۡتُمُ شَهَٰدَةَ ٱللَّهِ إِنَّآ إِذٗا لَّمِنَ ٱلۡأٓثِمِينَ ١٠٦\n(We will not withhold the testimony of [ordained by] Allah), the testimony of which Allah ordained to be guarded and given truly. In this verse, the testimony is linked to Allah to signify its importance. Ibn Juzay: 1/255.\nIn this verse, the testimony is linked to Allah. Why?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱسۡمَعُواْۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ١٠٨\n(And Fear Allah and listen): Listening obediently and accepting all commands. (For Allah does not guide the defiantly disobedient people) means that if you do not fear and listen, then you become defiantly disobedient and rouges whom Allah does not guide to the right way or to Paradise. Al-Alusi: 7/69.\nThis verse mentions a barrier to guidance and success. What is it?\nwords\nحَسبُنَاSufficient for us\nعَلَيكُم أَنفُسَكُمObligate yourselves to making good deeds\nضَرَبتُم فِي الأَرضِWhen you are traveling through the land\nالأَولَيَانِNearest in kin to the deceased"],[126,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nRead about the horrors of the Day of Resurrection and how people will be on that intense day.\nRead the story of Jesus (peace be upon him), and draw two lessons from it.\nThink of three favors that Allah blessed you with, then offer your thanks and gratitude to Him by words and deeds.\nguid\nIf the immensity of the Day of Resurrection and its hardships are manifested on the Messengers of Allah, then how is it going to be for the rest of the people?!\nAllah's favors on your parents or upon any one of them is also a favor upon you, so be thankful and grateful to Him.\nRemembering Allah's favors helps to offer thanks and gratitude to Him.\nrefl\nيَوۡمَ يَجۡمَعُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلرُّسُلَ فَيَقُولُ مَاذَآ أُجِبۡتُمۡۖ قَالُواْ لَا عِلۡمَ لَنَآۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّٰمُ ٱلۡغُيُوبِ ١٠٩\nMeaning: Did your nations accept or reject your message? Did they believe or disbelieve? The intended purpose of this question is a rebuke to those who disbelieved and so that they would be left with no excuse. Ibn Juzay: 1/256.\nWhat is the intended purpose for asking the Messengers about their nations?\nيَوۡمَ يَجۡمَعُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلرُّسُلَ فَيَقُولُ مَاذَآ أُجِبۡتُمۡۖ قَالُواْ لَا عِلۡمَ لَنَآۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّٰمُ ٱلۡغُيُوبِ ١٠٩\n(They will say, \"We have no knowledge\"), on the Day of Judgment, they will say that out of politeness with Allah by referring all knowledge to Him. Ibn Juzay: 1/256.\nThe Messengers will reply: (We have no knowledge). Why?\nيَوۡمَ يَجۡمَعُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلرُّسُلَ فَيَقُولُ مَاذَآ أُجِبۡتُمۡۖ قَالُواْ لَا عِلۡمَ لَنَآۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّٰمُ ٱلۡغُيُوبِ ١٠٩\nWhen they will say: (We have no knowledge), that does not mean a denial of their knowledge of what their nations did, rather they will be startled by the horror of that day. Then after their minds come back to them, they will answer and testify against their nations. Al-Tabari: 11/210.\nThe Messengers will reply with two answers. What are they? When will they be?\nإِذۡ قَالَ ٱللَّهُ يَٰعِيسَى ٱبۡنَ مَرۡيَمَ ٱذۡكُرۡ نِعۡمَتِي عَلَيۡكَ وَعَلَىٰ وَٰلِدَتِكَ إِذۡ أَيَّدتُّكَ بِرُوحِ ٱلۡقُدُسِ تُكَلِّمُ ٱلنَّاسَ فِي ٱلۡمَهۡدِ وَكَهۡلٗاۖ وَإِذۡ عَلَّمۡتُكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ وَٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةَ وَٱلۡإِنجِيلَۖ وَإِذۡ تَخۡلُقُ مِنَ ٱلطِّينِ كَهَيۡٔةِ ٱلطَّيۡرِ بِإِذۡنِي فَتَنفُخُ فِيهَا فَتَكُونُ طَيۡرَۢا بِإِذۡنِيۖ وَتُبۡرِئُ ٱلۡأَكۡمَهَ وَٱلۡأَبۡرَصَ بِإِذۡنِيۖ وَإِذۡ تُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡمَوۡتَىٰ بِإِذۡنِيۖ\nThis is a proof that Jesus (peace be upon him) was not a god, rather he was a servant of Allah, and he did all that only by Allah's permission, as did many Messengers before him. Here, it is quite clear that the one who gave the permission is other than the one who received it. Ibn Taimyah: 2/571.\nThis verse proves that Jesus (peace be upon him) was a servant of Allah, and not a god as Christians claim. How?\nٱذۡكُرۡ نِعۡمَتِي عَلَيۡكَ وَعَلَىٰ وَٰلِدَتِكَ\nMeaning: Remember it in your heart and verbally, and fulfill the obligation of giving thanks to your Lord, because He blessed you in ways in which He did not bless others. Al-Saadi: 248.\nDid Allah favor you with a special blessing? What is your duty toward that?\nوَإِذۡ تَخۡلُقُ مِنَ ٱلطِّينِ كَهَيۡـَٔةِ ٱلطَّيۡرِ بِإِذۡنِي فَتَنفُخُ فِيهَا فَتَكُونُ طَيۡرَۢا بِإِذۡنِيۖ وَتُبۡرِئُ ٱلۡأَكۡمَهَ وَٱلۡأَبۡرَصَ بِإِذۡنِيۖ وَإِذۡ تُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡمَوۡتَىٰ\n(By My permission), this statement is repeated with every miracle as a clear response to those who claim the lordship of Jesus. Ibn Juzay: 1/257.\nThis statement, (By My permission) is repeated with every miracle. Why?\nقَالُواْ نُرِيدُ أَن نَّأۡكُلَ مِنۡهَا وَتَطۡمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُنَا وَنَعۡلَمَ أَن قَدۡ صَدَقۡتَنَا وَنَكُونَ عَلَيۡهَا مِنَ ٱلشَّٰهِدِينَ ١١٣\nMeaning: We asked for it (a table spread with food) because we want to eat from it only for the blessing and not because we are hungry. We want to witness the Might of Allah, to let our hearts be reassured and to know that you are a Messenger of Allah so that our faith becomes steadfast. Al-Baghawi: 1/732.\nWhy did the disciples ask Jesus (peace be upon him) for a table spread with food?\nwords\nأَيَّدتُّكَI Had supported you\nبِرُوحِ القُدُسِThe angel Gabriel\nالأكمَهَA one who is born blind\nالحَوَارِيُّونَThe disciples of Jesus (peace be upon him)"],[127,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nRepeat this supplication today: \"O Allah, grant me provision, for You are the Best of Providers,\" as the Prophets (p) said before.\nRepeat this verse tonight, and reflect on its meanings as the Prophet (ﷺ) did.\nAsk Allah to make you truthful in your words and actions.\nguid\nIf you make a covenant with Allah and He grants you what you asked for, then beware of breaking your covenant because that would entail His severe punishment.\nBeing polite and humble in your speech with Allah, the Almighty, is a sign of your true faith.\nTruthfulness is a great virtue which is beneficial in this life and the Hereafter.\nrefl\nقَالَ ٱللَّهُ إِنِّي مُنَزِّلُهَا عَلَيۡكُمۡۖ فَمَن يَكۡفُرۡ بَعۡدُ مِنكُمۡ فَإِنِّيٓ أُعَذِّبُهُۥ عَذَابٗا لَّآ أُعَذِّبُهُۥٓ أَحَدٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١١٥\nAbdullah bin Omar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \"The severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection will be for whoever disbelieved among those who received the table spread with food, the people of Pharaoh and the hypocrites.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/258.\nDisbelieving after witnessing the signs is a greater sin than disbelieving at the outset. Explain.\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ ٱللَّهُ يَٰعِيسَى ٱبۡنَ مَرۡيَمَ ءَأَنتَ قُلۡتَ لِلنَّاسِ ٱتَّخِذُونِي وَأُمِّيَ إِلَٰهَيۡنِ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِۖ قَالَ سُبۡحَٰنَكَ مَا يَكُونُ لِيٓ أَنۡ أَقُولَ مَا لَيۡسَ لِي بِحَقٍّۚ إِن كُنتُ قُلۡتُهُۥ فَقَدۡ عَلِمۡتَهُۥۚ تَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي نَفۡسِي وَلَآ أَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي نَفۡسِكَۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّٰمُ ٱلۡغُيُوبِ ١١٦\n(Had I said so, You would have surely known it), an apology and disassociation from that claim. Jesus (peace be upon him) entrusts all knowledge to Allah so that his innocence will come out since Allah knows that he did not say that. Ibn Juzay: 1/259.\nDescribe Jesus (peace be upon him) politeness with Allah in three points?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ ٱللَّهُ يَٰعِيسَى ٱبۡنَ مَرۡيَمَ ءَأَنتَ قُلۡتَ لِلنَّاسِ ٱتَّخِذُونِي وَأُمِّيَ إِلَٰهَيۡنِ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِۖ قَالَ سُبۡحَٰنَكَ مَا يَكُونُ لِيٓ أَنۡ أَقُولَ مَا لَيۡسَ لِي بِحَقٍّۚ\nJesus (peace be upon him) will begin his reply with glorifying Allah for two reasons, first: Exalting Allah above all what is said. Second: Submitting to His Might and fearing His Power. Al-Qurtubi: 8/302.\nJesus (peace be upon him) will begin his reply with glorifying Allah. Why? What do we learn from that?\nإِن كُنتُ قُلۡتُهُۥ فَقَدۡ عَلِمۡتَهُۥۚ تَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي نَفۡسِي وَلَآ أَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي نَفۡسِكَۚ\nJesus (peace be upon him) will specify his \"self\" because it is the most likely place for hiding thoughts and information. Ibn Atiyah: 2/263.\nJesus (peace be upon him) will specify his \"self\", why?\nإِن تُعَذِّبۡهُمۡ فَإِنَّهُمۡ عِبَادُكَۖ وَإِن تَغۡفِرۡ لَهُمۡ فَإِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ١١٨\nIn his response, Jesus (peace be upon him) will not say, \"The Forgiving, The Merciful\" due to his politeness and humbleness in his speech with Allah who is angry with them and is about to send them to Hellfire. This is not a time for intercession, rather, it is time for disowning them. It means that if You forgive them, then Your forgiveness would be based upon Your perfect knowledge and power, and not due to incapability of punishing them or heedlessness of their crimes. Ibn Al-Qayim: 1/337.\nJesus (peace be upon him) will say: (the Exalted in Might, the Wise) and will not say: \"The Forgiving, The Merciful.\" Why?\nقَالَ ٱللَّهُ هَٰذَا يَوۡمُ يَنفَعُ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ صِدۡقُهُمۡۚ لَهُمۡ جَنَّٰتٞ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدٗاۖ رَّضِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَرَضُواْ عَنۡهُۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡفَوۡزُ ٱلۡعَظِيمُ ١١٩\n(Allah will say, \"This is the Day when the truthfulness of the truthful will benefit them\"), this statement includes all truthful believers but especially Jesus (peace be upon him) since it indicates his truthfulness which Allah bears witness to. Ibn Juzay: 1/260.\nThis verse shows the virtue of truthfulness. Explain.\nقَالَ ٱللَّهُ هَٰذَا يَوۡمُ يَنفَعُ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ صِدۡقُهُمۡۚ\nThis statement includes every believer in Allah, and the more righteous he is, the more included he will be. Moreover, the statement confirms the truthfulness of Jesus (u) which will give him an honorable status on that day. Ibn Atiyah: 2/263.\nTruthfulness is a salvation in this life and the Hereafter. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nتَكُونُ لَنَا عِيدًاWe will mark its day as a feast for us and for those who would come afterwards\nوَآيَةً مِنكَA sign of Your Oneness and Prophethood of Jesus (peace be upon him)\nشَهِيدًاA witness"],[128,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nDo a good deed in private today for the sake of Allah.\nIdentify three causes for the destruction of previous nations.\nTry to link a sin you had committed to a misfortune that struck you.\nguid\nPraise Allah abundantly and be grateful to Him because it is a great act of worship which draws you closer to Him.\nDisdaining and ridiculing religion is a cause for an imminent punishment.\nA disaster does not strike but due to a sin, and it is not lifted but with repentance.\nrefl\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ وَجَعَلَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ وَٱلنُّورَۖ ثُمَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِرَبِّهِمۡ يَعۡدِلُونَ ١\nThe scholars said: \"This Surah, (Al-An'am), was revealed as a whole at once because it is the basis on which debating polytheists, innovators (misguided in interpreting Sharia), and those who deny resurrection—is founded.\" Al-Qurtubi: 8/312.\nWhy was Surat (Al-An'am) revealed as a whole at once?\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ وَجَعَلَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ وَٱلنُّورَۖ ثُمَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِرَبِّهِمۡ يَعۡدِلُونَ ١\nMeaning: Be sincere in offering your praise and gratitude to the One Who created you all, the heavens and earth. Do not associate with Him anyone or anything since He is the only worthy of your praises due to His favors upon you and not those whom you are worshiping and associating with Him. Al-Tabari: 11/247.\nWhy should one be sincere in praising Allah?\nوَجَعَلَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ وَٱلنُّورَۖ\nIn the Arabic text, Allah mentions darkness in a plural form because there are so many different types of darkness, but He mentions light in a singular form, because the path that leads to Allah is one, not many. It is the path that requires knowledge of the truth and acting upon it. Al-Saadi: 250.\nDarkness is mentioned in a plural form while light is mentioned in a singular form. Why?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَكُم مِّن طِينٖ ثُمَّ قَضَىٰٓ أَجَلٗاۖ وَأَجَلٞ مُّسَمًّى عِندَهُۥۖ ثُمَّ أَنتُمۡ تَمۡتَرُونَ ٢\nAllah describes the term for resurrection as (known only to Him) because He kept the knowledge of the Hour unto Himself. Ibn Atiyah: 2/267.\nAllah describes the term for resurrection as (known only to Him.) Why?\nوَمَا تَأۡتِيهِم مِّنۡ ءَايَةٖ مِّنۡ ءَايَٰتِ رَبِّهِمۡ إِلَّا كَانُواْ عَنۡهَا مُعۡرِضِينَ ٤\nTurning away by neglecting to reflect on the signs that will lead them to the Oneness of Allah, such as the creation of heavens, earth and everything in between. Al-Baghawi: 2/10.\nHow is turning away from the signs of Allah, the Almighty, come about?\nأَلَمۡ يَرَوۡاْ كَمۡ أَهۡلَكۡنَا مِن قَبۡلِهِم مِّن قَرۡنٖ مَّكَّنَّٰهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ مَا لَمۡ نُمَكِّن لَّكُمۡ وَأَرۡسَلۡنَا ٱلسَّمَآءَ عَلَيۡهِم مِّدۡرَارٗا وَجَعَلۡنَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرَ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهِمۡ فَأَهۡلَكۡنَٰهُم بِذُنُوبِهِمۡ وَأَنشَأۡنَا مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡ قَرۡنًا ءَاخَرِينَ ٦\nTherefore, beware of the same end that might befall you, for you are not dearer to Allah than these previous nations, but the Messenger whom you defied is dearer to Allah than the Messengers they defied. Thus, you are more liable than them to receive torment, if it was not for Allah's mercy and kindness. Ibn Kathir: 2/117.\nWhat is Allah's way with societies whose evil is more than good?\nفَأَهۡلَكۡنَٰهُم بِذُنُوبِهِمۡ وَأَنشَأۡنَا مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡ قَرۡنًا ءَاخَرِينَ ٦\nMeaning: We had given them abundance of favors but they were ungrateful. (Then We destroyed them for their sins), they were destroyed for their disbelief because sins are the cause of punishment and cessation of favors. (and brought forth after them other generations): We created new generation afterward, thus, let these be warned of destruction too. Al-Qurtubi: 8/326.\nWhat is the cause for Allah's punishment?\nwords\nوَجَعَلَHe Created\nيَعدِلُونَThe disbelievers set up equals to their Lord\nتَمتَرُونَYou doubt\nوَهُوَ اللَّهُAnd He is Allah, the only deity Who is rightfully worshipped\nقَرنٍA generation of people\nمِدرَارًاAbundant rain\nلاَ يُنظَرُونَThey would not be given any respite"],[129,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you warn against the risk of ridiculing others, specially the righteous ones.\nKeep in mind that Allah Has taken it upon Himself to be Merciful, so ask humbly for His Mercy, and to make you merciful toward others.\nIf you become tempted today to commit a sin, then say this repeatedly: [Say, \"Indeed I fear, if I should disobey my Lord, the punishment of a tremendous Day\"].\nguid\nDo not take a protector whom you worship and entrust all matters to except Allah.\nIf you are ridiculed by someone, just remember that the Messengers were ridiculed before, so do not be distressed, for the best outcome is for those who fear Allah.\nHasten to abide by Allah's commands.\nrefl\nقُلۡ سِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ ثُمَّ ٱنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡمُكَذِّبِينَ ١١\nMeaning: If you doubt that, then travel through the land and see what was the fate of the deniers, for you will never find anything but people who were destroyed. The kind of travel enjoined here is travel in both a spiritual and physical sense, which will lead to drawing lessons; as for merely looking without learning any lesson, that is of no benefit. Al-Saadi: 251.\nWhat is the difference between a believer and a disbeliever when witnessing the ruins of destroyed nations?\nقُل لِّمَن مَّا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ قُل لِّلَّهِۚ كَتَبَ عَلَىٰ نَفۡسِهِ ٱلرَّحۡمَةَۚ لَيَجۡمَعَنَّكُمۡ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ لَا رَيۡبَ فِيهِۚ ٱلَّذِينَ خَسِرُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ فَهُمۡ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ ١٢\nThis is a gentle call from Allah to those who are turned away to come back to Him by stating that He is Merciful to His servants, does not rush to punish the guilty, and accepts their return in repentance. Al-Baghawi: 2/10.\nWhat is the intended meaning of this verse?\nقُل لِّمَن مَّا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ قُل لِّلَّهِۚ كَتَبَ عَلَىٰ نَفۡسِهِ ٱلرَّحۡمَةَۚ\nAllah extended His mercy and kindness to all of them; He encompassed them in His mercy and blessings, and He took it upon Himself and decreed for Himself that His mercy should take precedence over His wrath, and that giving is dearer to Him than withholding. Allah Has opened the gates of mercy to all of His servants, unless they close the gates to themselves by sinning; He Has called them to His mercy unless they are prevented from seeking it by their sins and faults. Al-Saadi: 251.\nWhat prevents a servant from benefiting from Allah's mercy?\nقُل لِّمَن مَّا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ قُل لِّلَّهِۚ كَتَبَ عَلَىٰ نَفۡسِهِ ٱلرَّحۡمَةَۚ\nOne may wonder: If Allah Has the dominion of heavens and earth, why does not He rush to punish those who live in His dominion yet associate partners with Him? A disbeliever may say: \"If what you said is true, then Allah would have punished us!\" On the other hand, the believer finds slow the coming of punishment of those disbelievers. Hence, Allah answers both by saying: (He has taken it upon Himself to be Merciful), by his grace, his mercy consists of a complete mercy for all of His believing servants, and a transient mercy which is a respite for the disbelievers. Ibn Ashur: 7/151.\nWhat is the link between this verse (He has taken it upon Himself to be Merciful) and the verse before?\nوَلَهُۥ مَا سَكَنَ فِي ٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِۚ وَهُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ١٣\nResting is singled out for mention because it manifests a greater blessing. Al-Baghawi: 2/11.\nWhy is resting singled out for mention?\nقُلۡ إِنِّيٓ أُمِرۡتُ أَنۡ أَكُونَ أَوَّلَ مَنۡ أَسۡلَمَۖ وَلَا تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١٤\nBeing (The first to submit) may refer to strength and steadfastness since the first person in any action usually is the most dedicated and attached to it, as Allah says about Moses (peace be upon him), (And I am the first of the believers) [7:143]. It is well-known that Moses (peace be upon him) was the first believer, but he meant that after falling unconscious, his faith became the firmest among people. Ibn Ashur: 7/158.\nWhat is meant by (The first)? What can you learn from that?\nوَإِن يَمۡسَسۡكَ ٱللَّهُ بِضُرّٖ فَلَا كَاشِفَ لَهُۥٓ إِلَّا هُوَۖ وَإِن يَمۡسَسۡكَ بِخَيۡرٖ فَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ١٧\nAllah says, (He is Most Capable of all things) after saying, (and if He grants you good) to indicate that His favors and blessings cannot be prevented by anyone; similarly, He says, (And if He wants good for you, none can withhold His bounty) [10:107]. Al-Shanqiti: 1/475.\nThe verse concludes with: (He is Most Capable of all things). Why?\nwords\nوَلَلَبَسنَاWe would have caused them confusion\nفَحَاقَOverwhelmed\nيَمسَسكَAfflicts you"],[130,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nToday, repeat this supplication: \"My Lord, increase my knowledge.\"\nRecall an issue in religion that you did not fully comprehend, then ask often for Allah's forgiveness so that you may be able to understand it better.\nVisit a graveyard or recall an image of a grave, then reflect on this verse\nguid\nBeing dishonest with yourself by belittling your sins and neglecting your duties will not save you on the Day of Resurrection because that is when the truth comes out.\nFalsehood and fabrications will vanish from their owner on the Day of Resurrection.\nCommitting sins impedes one's understanding of the words of Allah.\nrefl\nقُلۡ أَيُّ شَيۡءٍ أَكۡبَرُ شَهَٰدَةٗۖ قُلِ ٱللَّهُۖ شَهِيدُۢ بَيۡنِي وَبَيۡنَكُمۡۚ\nMeaning: Allah testifies for me by means of His approval and His actions; He supports me in what I say to you. Allah is Most Wise, All-Powerful, so it is not befitting His wisdom and might to let one who is lying about Him and claiming that Allah sent him when He did not, or that Allah commanded him to call people when He did not, and that Allah permitted him to fight those who oppose him, get carried away (and not seize or punish him). Yet, He confirms that he is speaking the truth by allowing him to carry on and supporting him in what he says by dazzling miracles and clear signs, and He helps him and causes the efforts of those who oppose him to end in failure. What testimony could be greater than this testimony. Al-Saadi: 252-253.\nWhat is meant by: Allah is Witness between the Messenger and those who rejected him?\nوَأُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانُ لِأُنذِرَكُم بِهِۦ وَمَنۢ بَلَغَۚ\nThe Messenger (ﷺ) was commanded to convey this Quran to the closest to him by kinship and place, then to other groups, one after the other until it reaches all mankind on earth as Allah says, (This Quran has been revealed to me so that I may warn you thereby); therefore, whoever is reached by the Quran, is considered warned by the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ). Ibn Taimyah: 3/20.\nConveying the message of Islam is the Muslim's duty. How can that be achieved?\nوَأُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانُ لِأُنذِرَكُم بِهِۦ وَمَنۢ بَلَغَۚ\n(This Quran has been revealed to me so that I may warn you thereby) to warn you of Allah's punishment, and warn others who may receive it that if they do not abide by the rules of the Quran, the lawful, the unlawful, and believe in everything else in the Quran, then they will be subject to Allah's punishment. Al-Tabari: 11/290.\nThe ultimate aim of revealing the Holy Quran is adhering to its rules. Explain.\nٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ كَذَبُواْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡۚ وَضَلَّ عَنۡهُم مَّا كَانُواْ يَفۡتَرُونَ ٢٤\n(Will vanish from them), their fabrication will fade away from them. (What they used to fabricate) such as idols which they hoped for their intercession and help, but all will be abolished on the Last Day. Al-Baghawi: 2/14.\nHow will their fabrication and falsehood vanish from them?\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَسۡتَمِعُ إِلَيۡكَۖ وَجَعَلۡنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ أَكِنَّةً أَن يَفۡقَهُوهُ وَفِيٓ ءَاذَانِهِمۡ وَقۡرٗاۚ\nMeaning: Among the polytheists, there are people who sometimes, for some reason, find themselves listening to what you say, but it is listening that is devoid of any quest for the truth. Hence, they do not benefit from listening, because they are not seeking to follow what is right. (But We have placed covers on their hearts), covers and layers lest they understand the word of Allah; He Has protected His word from such people. Al-Saadi: 254.\nIs being away from the Quran considered a punishment from Allah? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَجَعَلۡنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ أَكِنَّةً أَن يَفۡقَهُوهُ وَفِيٓ ءَاذَانِهِمۡ وَقۡرٗاۚ وَإِن يَرَوۡاْ كُلَّ ءَايَةٖ لَّا يُؤۡمِنُواْ بِهَاۖ\n(But We have placed covers on their hearts so that they do not understand it), Allah Has put these caps on their hearts as a barrier between them and understanding the Quran whenever they listened to its recital. The Arabic words for \"covers\" and \"deafness\" are: (Akennah) and (waqr), and they are used here to add intensity. Ibn Juzay: 1/266.\nThe disbelievers cannot benefit from the Quran. Why?\nوَهُمۡ يَنۡهَوۡنَ عَنۡهُ وَيَنۡـَٔوۡنَ عَنۡهُۖ وَإِن يُهۡلِكُونَ إِلَّآ أَنفُسَهُمۡ وَمَا يَشۡعُرُونَ ٢٦\nThe evil consequence of their actions will come back to them along with the burdens of those whom they misled, (but they do not realize). Al-Baghawi: 2/16.\nA person may bear the burden of his sins and the sins of others. How?\nwords\nفِتنَتُهُمTheir response\nأَكِنَّةًCovers\nوَقرًاDeafness\nأَسَاطِيرُ الأَوَّلِينَAncient fables\nوَيَنأَونَThey keep away"],[131,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nIncrease your good deeds today, and perform voluntary prayer so you will not regret your carelessness on the Day of Resurrection.\nThink of an act of worship that you wish to do but you had postponed, and do it today.\nInvite a relative or a friend to do a good deed, and endure his rejection.\nguid\nSins are the worst burden for one to carry on the Day of Resurrection.\nThe Holy Quran preaches wise people not to be deceived by this worldly life and neglect working for the Hereafter which is best for them.\nAnyone who calls others to Allah should not be surprised by people rejection since the Messengers were rejected by people before.\nrefl\nبَلۡ بَدَا لَهُم مَّا كَانُواْ يُخۡفُونَ مِن قَبۡلُۖ وَلَوۡ رُدُّواْ لَعَادُواْ لِمَا نُهُواْ عَنۡهُ وَإِنَّهُمۡ لَكَٰذِبُونَ ٢٨\nShirk, which is associating partners with Allah will become apparent to them so they will say: (By Allah, our Lord, we never associated any partners (with Allah)), then Allah will make their senses to speak and they will testify against them. Al-Qurtubi: 8/354.\nWhat did they conceal before? How will it become apparent to them?\nوَمَا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَآ إِلَّا لَعِبٞ وَلَهۡوٞۖ وَلَلدَّارُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةُ خَيۡرٞ لِّلَّذِينَ يَتَّقُونَۚ أَفَلَا تَعۡقِلُونَ ٣٢\nThe reality of this world is that it is mere play and distraction; it is play in a physical sense, and its distraction affects hearts and minds, which are deeply attached to it, and focus all their attention on it, like children at play. As for the Hereafter, it is (best for those who fear Allah), in itself and in its attributes and eternal nature. In it, there is what hearts long for and what delights the eye of bliss, pleasure, happiness and joy. But that is not for everyone; rather it is only for those who fear Allah, comply with His commands and avoid what He prohibits. Al-Saadi: 252-253.\nList two differences between enjoyment of this world and the bliss of the Hereafter?\nوَمَا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَآ إِلَّا لَعِبٞ وَلَهۡوٞۖ وَلَلدَّارُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةُ خَيۡرٞ لِّلَّذِينَ يَتَّقُونَۚ أَفَلَا تَعۡقِلُونَ ٣٢\nIn this life, what is done for the sake of the Hereafter is not considered amusement or diversion. Amusement is doing something of no value, and diversion is doing something for distraction only. Ibn Abbas (t) said: \"This (amusement and diversion) is the life of the disbeliever because he spent it in delusion and falsehood, but the life of the believer is full of good deeds.\" Al-Qurtubi: 8/361.\nIs everything in this worldly life amusement and diversion?\nفَإِنَّهُمۡ لَا يُكَذِّبُونَكَ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ يَجۡحَدُونَ ٣٣\nAllah Has negated their doubt but confirmed their denial. It is well-known that doubting by their tongues was not repudiated, rather it was the doubt in their hearts that was negated, [i.e. they knew in their hearts that Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) was truthful]. Ibn Taimyah: 3/23.\nWhat is the negated doubt in this verse?\nوَلَقَدۡ كُذِّبَتۡ رُسُلٞ مِّن قَبۡلِكَ فَصَبَرُواْ عَلَىٰ مَا كُذِّبُواْ وَأُوذُواْ حَتَّىٰٓ أَتَىٰهُمۡ نَصۡرُنَاۚ\nTherefore, be patient as they were patient, and you will attain victory as they did. Al-Saadi: 255.\nWhat is the wisdom behind narrating the stories of previous Messengers?\nوَلَقَدۡ كُذِّبَتۡ رُسُلٞ مِّن قَبۡلِكَ فَصَبَرُواْ عَلَىٰ مَا كُذِّبُواْ وَأُوذُواْ حَتَّىٰٓ أَتَىٰهُمۡ نَصۡرُنَاۚ وَلَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمَٰتِ ٱللَّهِۚ وَلَقَدۡ جَآءَكَ مِن نَّبَإِيْ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٣٤\n(You have already received some accounts of those messengers), some of their news, which included their endurance then their triumph. This enforces the belief in Allah's promise and encourages patience. Ibn Juzay: 1/266.\nThe aim of revealing the Holy Quran is to adhere to its rules. Explain.\nوَإِن كَانَ كَبُرَ عَلَيۡكَ إِعۡرَاضُهُمۡ فَإِنِ ٱسۡتَطَعۡتَ أَن تَبۡتَغِيَ نَفَقٗا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ أَوۡ سُلَّمٗا فِي ٱلسَّمَآءِ فَتَأۡتِيَهُم بِـَٔايَةٖۚ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَجَمَعَهُمۡ عَلَى ٱلۡهُدَىٰۚ فَلَا تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡجَٰهِلِينَ ٣٥\nAllah commanded His Messenger (ﷺ) not to grieve for their disbelief since he did not have the power to guide them to the truth. Al-Qurtubi: 8/367.\nFor one who calls others to Allah, why should he not grieve for those who turn away?\nwords\nكَبُرَHard to bear"],[132,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nThink of a particular animal or a bird, and reflect on the fact that they are actually a community among other communities.\nReflect on the verses that you have heard today during the prayer and the commands and prohibitions they contain, then think which of them you applied.\nThink of an affliction that struck you and call persistently upon Allah to remove it.\nguid\nTrue guidance is from Allah, so seek guidance only from Him.\nSickness, poverty and other hardships may remind you of Allah and turn you back to Him.\nIf the easy life and abundance of bounties are accompanied with heedlessness, then it may be a prelude for destruction.\nrefl\nإِنَّمَا يَسۡتَجِيبُ ٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡمَعُونَۘ\nWhat is meant by listening in this case is listening with the heart and accepting; as for merely hearing, this is something that is done by both the righteous and the immoral. Proof is established against all those who are accountable when they hear the revelations of Allah, after which there is no excuse left for not accepting the message. Al-Saadi: 255.\nIn hearing sermons, what is the difference between the righteous and the heedless?\nوَٱلۡمَوۡتَىٰ يَبۡعَثُهُمُ ٱللَّهُ\nThis refers to the disbelievers because their hearts are dead, therefore, Allah resembles them to dead corpses. Ibn Kathir:2/124.\nWhat is the resemblance between a disbeliever and a dead person?\nمَّا فَرَّطۡنَا فِي ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مِن شَيۡءٖۚ ثُمَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ يُحۡشَرُونَ ٣٨\nAll things, great and small, are written in the Preserved Tablet (Al-Lawh Al-Mahfooth) as they are decreed, and all things will come to pass in accordance with what the Pen wrote. This verse indicates that the Preserved Tablet is the record of all things that will happen. This is the first stage of the divine Will and Decree, of which there are four stages: The all-encompassing knowledge of Allah; His Book that contains all that which exists; His Will that is applicable to all things; and His creation of all created things. Al-Saadi: 255.\nEverything that happens in your life goes through four stages. What are they?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَآ إِلَىٰٓ أُمَمٖ مِّن قَبۡلِكَ فَأَخَذۡنَٰهُم بِٱلۡبَأۡسَآءِ وَٱلضَّرَّآءِ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَضَرَّعُونَ ٤٢ فَلَوۡلَآ إِذۡ جَآءَهُم بَأۡسُنَا تَضَرَّعُواْ وَلَٰكِن قَسَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ مَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٤٣\nAllah Has censured two groups, first: Those who when they are struck with hardships, they do not plead with Allah, do not humble themselves to Him nor repent from their sins as Allah says, (And We sent messengers to nations before you and seized them with poverty and hardship, so that they may humble themselves ` If only they had humbled themselves when Our affliction came upon them, but their hearts were hardened, and satan made their misdeeds appealing to them). Second: Those who plead with Allah and repent to Him during hardships, but after He removes their hardships, they turn away. The praised group, however, are those who plead with Allah, and repent to Him at all times, during hardships and comfort. Ibn Taimyah: 3/24-25.\nList the situations of people during times of hardships and comfort?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَآ إِلَىٰٓ أُمَمٖ مِّن قَبۡلِكَ فَأَخَذۡنَٰهُم بِٱلۡبَأۡسَآءِ وَٱلضَّرَّآءِ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَضَرَّعُونَ ٤٢ فَلَوۡلَآ إِذۡ جَآءَهُم بَأۡسُنَا تَضَرَّعُواْ وَلَٰكِن قَسَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ مَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٤٣\n(And seized them with poverty and hardship), this was a disciplinary action. (If only they): this is an offer and encouragement, which proves that humbling oneself during hardships is beneficial. Ibn Juzay: 1/270.\nIn light of this verse, explain the importance of humbling oneself during hardships?\nفَلَمَّا نَسُواْ مَا ذُكِّرُواْ بِهِۦ فَتَحۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ أَبۡوَٰبَ كُلِّ شَيۡءٍ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فَرِحُواْ بِمَآ أُوتُوٓاْ أَخَذۡنَٰهُم بَغۡتَةٗ فَإِذَا هُم مُّبۡلِسُونَ ٤٤\nWe opened up the doors to everything that was closed to them before. (Until just when they were happiest with what they had been given) they became reckless and conceited, and thought that this bounty was endless and a sign of Allah's love for them. (We caught them): We destroyed them. (suddenly): abruptly and unexpectedly. Al-Qurtubi: 8/379.\nFrom this verse, describe how Allah gradually leads heedless people?\nفَلَمَّا نَسُواْ مَا ذُكِّرُواْ بِهِۦ فَتَحۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ أَبۡوَٰبَ كُلِّ شَيۡءٍ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فَرِحُواْ بِمَآ أُوتُوٓاْ أَخَذۡنَٰهُم بَغۡتَةٗ فَإِذَا هُم مُّبۡلِسُونَ ٤٤\nAl-Hasan Al-Basri said: \"Whomever Allah gives provision and he thinks that Allah is not testing him, has no wisdom. Whoever has little provision and thinks that Allah will not look at (provide for) him, has no wisdom.\" He then recited this verse. Ibn Kathir:2/126.\nHow does a Muslim deal with his financial fluctuations?\nwords\nمَا فَرَّطنَاWe have missed nothing\nصُمٌّDeaf\nوَبُكمٌDumb\nأَرَأَيتَكُمTell me\nمُبلِسُونَThey are left in despair"],[133,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nExplain to those around you the truth about fortune tellers and others who claim to predict future events that they, in fact, do not know the unseen.\nShare a message in which you cite an exhortation from the Holy Quran.\nSit down today with some righteous poor or weak people to soften your heart and learn modesty.\nguid\nThe demise of the wrongdoers is inevitable, sooner or later.\nUse glad tidings and warnings in your speech when inviting others to Allah.\nIf the Prophet (ﷺ) does not know the unseen, then, surely neither do those who are below him.\nrefl\nفَقُطِعَ دَابِرُ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْۚ وَٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٤٥\n(Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds), for He Has willed and decreed the destruction of the disbelievers, as this highlights His signs, honors His allies, humiliates His enemies and confirms the truthfulness of what the Messengers brought. Al-Saadi: 256.\nIn this verse, the destruction of polytheists is concluded with praising Allah. Why?\nفَقُطِعَ دَابِرُ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْۚ وَٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٤٥\nPraising Allah for the destruction of the wrongdoers is the right thing to do because with their absence, the lives of people become righteous, which is a blessing that entails giving praise to Allah. Ibn Ashur: 7/232.\nThe destruction of the wrongdoers is a blessing from Allah. Explain.\nفَقُطِعَ دَابِرُ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْۚ وَٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٤٥\nAllah praises Himself for the destruction of the wrongdoers because it is His favor upon His Messengers. So, Allah praises Himself to teach His Messengers and their followers to do the same and praise Him for ridding them of the wrongdoers' evil. Al-Baghawi: 2/22.\nWhat should we do when witnessing the demise of the wrongdoers?\nقُلۡ أَرَءَيۡتُمۡ إِنۡ أَخَذَ ٱللَّهُ سَمۡعَكُمۡ وَأَبۡصَٰرَكُمۡ وَخَتَمَ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِكُم مَّنۡ إِلَٰهٌ غَيۡرُ ٱللَّهِ يَأۡتِيكُم بِهِۗ ٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ نُصَرِّفُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ ثُمَّ هُمۡ يَصۡدِفُونَ ٤٦\nDiversifying the signs means different types of them, where they become evident as proofs from observations in the heavens and earth, proofs from within the souls of people, and other proofs from the affairs of previous nations. Ibn Ashur: 7/235.\nHow do signs that are mentioned in this verse become diversified?\nوَأَنذِرۡ بِهِ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخَافُونَ أَن يُحۡشَرُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ\nThis Quran is a warning to all people, but only (those who fear being gathered to their Lord) will benefit from it, for they are certain that they will move from this realm to the eternal realm of the Hereafter, and therefore they do what will benefit them and refrain from what will harm them. Al-Saadi: 257.\nWarning by the Quran is directed to those who fear being gathered before Allah. Why?\nوَلَا تَطۡرُدِ ٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ رَبَّهُم بِٱلۡغَدَوٰةِ وَٱلۡعَشِيِّ يُرِيدُونَ وَجۡهَهُۥۖ\nThese time periods, morning and evening are singled out for mention because they are normally busy times for most people, and whoever is worshiping Allah during these times, is more likely to do that during idle times. Al-Qurtubi: 8/389.\nIn this verse, morning and evening are singled out for mention. Why?\nوَلَا تَطۡرُدِ ٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ رَبَّهُم بِٱلۡغَدَوٰةِ وَٱلۡعَشِيِّ يُرِيدُونَ وَجۡهَهُۥۖ مَا عَلَيۡكَ مِنۡ حِسَابِهِم مِّن شَيۡءٖ وَمَا مِنۡ حِسَابِكَ عَلَيۡهِم مِّن شَيۡءٖ فَتَطۡرُدَهُمۡ فَتَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٥٢\nThis verse refers to the poor Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), such as Bilal, Ammar bin Yassir, Abdullah bin Masoud, Khabbab, Suhaib and others, when some polytheists said to the Prophet (ﷺ): \"We cannot sit with these people because of our high standing, so if you send them away, we will follow you.\" And so, this verse was revealed in response to their request. Ibn Juzay: 1/271.\nFor one who invites others to Allah, this verse sets an approach on how to deal with them. What is it?\nwords\nفَقُطِعَEliminated\nدَابِرُThe last remnant of them\nنُصَرِّفُWe diversify\nيَصدِفُونَThey turn away\nبِالغَدَاةِMorning"],[134,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nGive thanks to Allah for His favors, as offering gratitude to Him is the key to attaining guidance and provision.\nCall someone to the way of Allah by endearing Allah's mercy to him.\nThink of a sin that you had committed with ignorance and ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nguid\nAllah decreed Mercy upon Himself, so ask Him humbly for His mercy.\nThe Quran is the judge over people's ways and ideas, sorting out good from evil.\nThe patience and forbearance shown by one who call misguided people to the way of Allah is an act of worship that brings him closer to Allah.\nrefl\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ فَتَنَّا بَعۡضَهُم بِبَعۡضٖ لِّيَقُولُوٓاْ أَهَٰٓؤُلَآءِ مَنَّ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِم مِّنۢ بَيۡنِنَآۗ أَلَيۡسَ ٱللَّهُ بِأَعۡلَمَ بِٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ٥٣\n(Thus We have tested some of them by means of others), We tested the disbelievers by the believers, and that was when the disbelievers said: \"are these poor slaves chosen by Allah over us for truth and eternal bliss while we are the noble rich?\" They were dismissing this notion! So, Allah responded to them saying: (Does Allah not know best those who are grateful). Ibn Juzay: 1/271.\nThe guidance of poor slaves was a test for the disbelievers. How?\nأَلَيۡسَ ٱللَّهُ بِأَعۡلَمَ بِٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ٥٣\nThe \"grateful\" are those who appreciate the blessing of faith in Allah, and offer their gratitude to Him for that. Ibn Taimyah: 3/28.\nWhat is meant by the \"grateful\" in this verse?\nوَإِذَا جَآءَكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا فَقُلۡ سَلَٰمٌ عَلَيۡكُمۡۖ كَتَبَ رَبُّكُمۡ عَلَىٰ نَفۡسِهِ ٱلرَّحۡمَةَ أَنَّهُۥ مَنۡ عَمِلَ مِنكُمۡ سُوٓءَۢا بِجَهَٰلَةٖ ثُمَّ تَابَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ وَأَصۡلَحَ فَأَنَّهُۥ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٥٤\nMeaning: When the believers come to you, greet them and welcome them warmly, and say things to raise their morale and motivate them, tell them of the mercy, bounty and kindness of Allah, and encourage them by all means that may achieve that; and warn them against committing sins and persisting therein, and instruct them to repent from sins, so that they may attain the forgiveness and bounty of their Lord. Al-Saadi: 258.\nHow should the scholars and preachers deal with their righteous followers?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ وَلِتَسۡتَبِينَ سَبِيلُ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ ٥٥\nWhen the way of evildoers becomes known, then the way of the believers are also known. Al-Qurtubi: 8/396.\nAllah mentions the way of the evildoers and not that of the believers. Why ?\nوَلِتَسۡتَبِينَ سَبِيلُ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ ٥٥\nOnce the way of the evildoers is made clear, it can be avoided, unlike when it remains indistinct and ambiguous, in which case this noble goal [of avoiding it] cannot be attained. Al-Saadi: 258.\nWhat is the wisdom behind clarifying the ways of the evildoers?\nقُل لَّوۡ أَنَّ عِندِي مَا تَسۡتَعۡجِلُونَ بِهِۦ لَقُضِيَ ٱلۡأَمۡرُ بَيۡنِي وَبَيۡنَكُمۡۗ\nMeaning: I would have brought it upon you and there would be nothing good for you in that, but the matter is in the Hand of the Most Forbearing, Most Patient, Whom people disobey in the most audacious manner, yet He grants them well-being and provision, and bestows His blessings, both apparent and hidden, upon them. Al-Saadi: 259.\nThis verse describes the great mercy of Allah, the Almighty, how?\nوَعِندَهُۥ مَفَاتِحُ ٱلۡغَيۡبِ لَا يَعۡلَمُهَآ إِلَّا هُوَۚ وَيَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي ٱلۡبَرِّ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِۚ وَمَا تَسۡقُطُ مِن وَرَقَةٍ إِلَّا يَعۡلَمُهَا\n(And not a leaf falls but that He knows it), Allah knows when and where a tree leaf falls, and how long it stays airborne before reaching the ground. He knows when every grain will grow, how much it will grow and who will eat from it. Al-Qurtubi: 8/405.\nThis verse states an example of the limitless knowledge of Allah. Explain.\nwords\nفَتَنَّاWe tested\nبِجَهَالَةٍOut of ignorance, every sinner is ignorant\nمَفَاتِحُ الغَيبِKeys of the unseen, (five keys listed at the end of Surat Luqman)"],[135,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nInvoke Allah humbly to ease your hardship, and grant you your wish, as there is no one who can save you from hardships but Him.\nReconcile between two feuding individuals or groups.\nShare a message in which you warn against media platforms that slander religion.\nguid\nWarn against disagreements that lead to division and dispute.\nStay away from places of ill speech and falsehood.\nThere are angels who watch over you, and record your words and actions, so beware of what you say and do.\nrefl\nوَهُوَ أَسۡرَعُ ٱلۡحَٰسِبِينَ ٦٢\nAllah is the Swiftest Reckoner because of His perfect knowledge, and His keeping of their deeds in the Preserved Tablet, then it is written again by the angels in the records that they keep. Al-Saadi: 259.\nAllah's greatness is manifested in Him being the Swiftest Reckoner. Explain.\nقُلۡ مَن يُنَجِّيكُم مِّن ظُلُمَٰتِ ٱلۡبَرِّ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِ تَدۡعُونَهُۥ تَضَرُّعٗا وَخُفۡيَةٗ لَّئِنۡ أَنجَىٰنَا مِنۡ هَٰذِهِۦ لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ٦٣\n(We will certainly be among those who are grateful), gratitude is recognizing Allah's favor, and fulfilling one's duty toward Him. Al-Baghawi: 2/30.\nHow can one attain a full gratitude for Allah's favors?\nقُلۡ مَن يُنَجِّيكُم مِّن ظُلُمَٰتِ ٱلۡبَرِّ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِ تَدۡعُونَهُۥ تَضَرُّعٗا وَخُفۡيَةٗ لَّئِنۡ أَنجَىٰنَا مِنۡ هَٰذِهِۦ لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ٦٣ قُلِ ٱللَّهُ يُنَجِّيكُم مِّنۡهَا وَمِن كُلِّ كَرۡبٖ ثُمَّ أَنتُمۡ تُشۡرِكُونَ ٦٤\nAllah rebukes them for invoking Him during hardship, then when in comfort, they associate others with Him. Al-Qurtubi: 8/412.\nThe polytheists contradiction is clear in this verse. Explain in light of this verse.\nأَوۡ يَلۡبِسَكُمۡ شِيَعٗا وَيُذِيقَ بَعۡضَكُم بَأۡسَ بَعۡضٍۗ\n(Or split you into factions), it is said that Allah will split you into different groups, fighting each other, by effecting disagreement among your leaders over worldly gains and that what is meant by this verse, (and make you suffer at the hands of one another) through war and killing during turmoil. Al-Qurtubi: 8/414.\nHow is a society punished by splitting it into factions?\nوَإِذَا رَأَيۡتَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخُوضُونَ فِيٓ ءَايَٰتِنَا فَأَعۡرِضۡ عَنۡهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ يَخُوضُواْ فِي حَدِيثٍ غَيۡرِهِۦۚ وَإِمَّا يُنسِيَنَّكَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فَلَا تَقۡعُدۡ بَعۡدَ ٱلذِّكۡرَىٰ مَعَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٦٨\nIf satan made you forget this prohibited company of wrongdoers, then do not remain with them after remembering that. Ibn Juzay: 1/274.\nWhat is your advice to one who sits with those who ridicule verses of Allah under the pretense of awareness and enlightenment?\nوَإِذَا رَأَيۡتَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخُوضُونَ فِيٓ ءَايَٰتِنَا فَأَعۡرِضۡ عَنۡهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ يَخُوضُواْ فِي حَدِيثٍ غَيۡرِهِۦۚ وَإِمَّا يُنسِيَنَّكَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فَلَا تَقۡعُدۡ بَعۡدَ ٱلذِّكۡرَىٰ مَعَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٦٨\nWhoever ridicules the verses of Allah, whether a believer or a disbeliever, must be abandoned. Al-Qurtubi: 8/419.\nWhat must be our stance on one who promotes doubts and religious innovations?\nوَإِمَّا يُنسِيَنَّكَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فَلَا تَقۡعُدۡ بَعۡدَ ٱلذِّكۡرَىٰ مَعَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٦٨\nFailing to remember to do the right thing is from satan as Allah says, (If satan should make you forget, then as soon as you remember, do not remain with the wrongdoing people). Ibn Taimyah: 3/32.\nHow does one forget to do the right thing?\nwords\nجَرَحتُمYou have committed\nلاَ يُفَرِّطُونَThey never fail nor fall short in their duty\nيَلبِسَكُم شِيَعًاHe splits you into factions\nنُصَرِّفُWe diversify\nيَخُوضُونَThose who ridicule"],[136,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nThink of a distracting gathering that you go to regularly, and substitute it with a useful one.\nSend this verse to those who invoke the dead.\nSeek refuge with Allah from devils' temptation that turns away from the path of Allah, and ask Allah to keep you firm on His way until you meet Him.\nguid\nIf one enjoins what is right, forbids what is evil and turns away from those who commit major sins, then there is no blame on him.\nBeware of taking the religion as a subject for joking and amusement. Religion is a great matter to Allah.\nOne of the best means to invite others to the path of Allah is speaking about the Holy Quran and its verses.\nrefl\nوَمَا عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ يَتَّقُونَ مِنۡ حِسَابِهِم مِّن شَيۡءٖ وَلَٰكِن ذِكۡرَىٰ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَّقُونَ ٦٩\nThis indicates that anyone who wants to remind others of Allah, should use words that are most likely to help them attain piety. Al-Saadi: 261.\nWhat should be the aim of the one who reminds others of Allah?\nوَذَرِ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُواْ دِينَهُمۡ لَعِبٗا وَلَهۡوٗا وَغَرَّتۡهُمُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۚ\nIf you are commanded to admonish those who are stubborn, then do not preoccupy yourself with them. (Amusement and diversion), which means ridiculing the religion to which you called them. It is also said that they ridiculed their own religion, and did not adhere to it. Ridiculing any religion is not justified. Al-Qurtubi: 8/423.\nHow is Allah's religion taken as amusement and diversion?\nوَذَرِ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُواْ دِينَهُمۡ لَعِبٗا وَلَهۡوٗا وَغَرَّتۡهُمُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۚ\nThe mention of (life) here indicates an important fact that all they cared about was life itself, and not earning good deeds which leads to the bliss of the Hereafter. This life had deceived them and made them think that there was no life after it. Ibn Ashur: 7/296.\nWhat is the reason for mentioning (life) in this verse?\nوَذَكِّرۡ بِهِۦٓ\nMeaning: Remind with the Quran through mentioning what will benefit people, enjoining, explaining and presenting it in an attractive manner by referring to its beauty. Moreover, mention what is harmful to people, and warn them against doing it, clarifying its various types, and what is bad about it, which will prompt people to refrain from it. Al-Saadi: 261.\nWhat is the ideal approach to use the Holy Quran in inviting others to the way of Allah?\nوَذَكِّرۡ بِهِۦٓ أَن تُبۡسَلَ نَفۡسُۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتۡ\nMeaning: A soul is bounded and constrained from what saves it in this life and in the Hereafter. Sins are like shackles that hold down its perpetrator, and keep him from being able to seek faith in the Oneness of Allah. In the Hereafter, sins prevent him from receiving the reward for good deeds, and so he is, in fact, bounded in this life and in the Hereafter. Ibn Taimyah: 3/33.\nSins are like shackles to the sinner. Explain in light of this verse.\nقُلۡ أَنَدۡعُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا يَنفَعُنَا وَلَا يَضُرُّنَا وَنُرَدُّ عَلَىٰٓ أَعۡقَابِنَا بَعۡدَ إِذۡ هَدَىٰنَا ٱللَّهُ كَٱلَّذِي ٱسۡتَهۡوَتۡهُ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينُ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ حَيۡرَانَ لَهُۥٓ أَصۡحَٰبٞ يَدۡعُونَهُۥٓ إِلَى ٱلۡهُدَى ٱئۡتِنَاۗ\nSome of the people will follow their inclination toward guidance in all or most of their affairs, and some will do the opposite of that while others will be inclined equally toward both, and will experience inner conflict. Thus, you recognize those who are destined for Paradise and those who are destined for Hellfire. Al-Saadi: 261-262.\nThere are three types of people when it comes to dealing with a caller to guidance. What are they? Among which type do you hope to be?\nكَٱلَّذِي ٱسۡتَهۡوَتۡهُ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينُ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ حَيۡرَانَ لَهُۥٓ أَصۡحَٰبٞ يَدۡعُونَهُۥٓ إِلَى ٱلۡهُدَى ٱئۡتِنَاۗ قُلۡ إِنَّ هُدَى ٱللَّهِ هُوَ ٱلۡهُدَىٰۖ وَأُمِرۡنَا لِنُسۡلِمَ لِرَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٧١\n(Although he has companions), these are the good company who invite him to guidance, and say, \"Come to us\", but he is lost and went far away that he did not respond to them. This is a representation of a misguided person who is being called to guidance but does not respond. Ibn Juzay: 1/275.\nFrom this verse, who is the bewildered?\nwords\nتُبسَلَBounded [by what it earned]\nتَعدِلOffers a ransom\nأُبسِلُواThey will be bounded by their sins\nحَمِيمٍScalding water\nاستَهوَتهُTempted (by devils)\nالصُّورِThe horn which is blown by angel Israfil"],[137,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nForbid an act of evil, even if it is from the closest people to you, and offer them advice in a wise manner that would make it acceptable to them.\nAsk Allah to be among those who have certain faith.\nShare a message in which you advise grave worshipers and remind them of this sacred verse.\nguid\nAllah gives His guidance to whom He chooses.\nStrive to achieve certain faith, as it is one of the noblest and highest levels of faith. Reflecting on the signs is a means to reach certain faith.\nPolytheists are filled with cowardice and fear while sincere believers are the most secure and resolute.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمُ لِأَبِيهِ ءَازَرَ أَتَتَّخِذُ أَصۡنَامًا ءَالِهَةً إِنِّيٓ أَرَىٰكَ وَقَوۡمَكَ فِي ضَلَٰلٖ مُّبِينٖ ٧٤\nThis does not contravene Abraham's kindness to his father since speaking the truth without insult or abuse does not contradict kindness. Ibn Ashur: 7/314.\nFrom this verse, did Abraham (peace be upon him) say something that contravene kindness to his father? Explain.\nفَلَمَّا جَنَّ عَلَيۡهِ ٱلَّيۡلُ رَءَا كَوۡكَبٗاۖ قَالَ هَٰذَا رَبِّيۖ فَلَمَّآ أَفَلَ قَالَ لَآ أُحِبُّ ٱلۡأٓفِلِينَ ٧٦\nThe essence of worship is love, and association in love is association in worship, as Allah says about His Prophet Abraham (peace be upon him), (So when the night grew dark upon him, he saw a star and said, \"This is my Lord.\" But when it set, he said, \"I do not like those that set). Ibn Taimyah: 3/34.\nLove which is the essence of worship, ignorant people made it an essence of shirk. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالَ هَٰذَا رَبِّيۖ\nGoing along with his opponent's argument, he said: This is my lord, so let us see whether it is deserving of lordship or not, and whether there will be any proof for that, as it is not appropriate for the wise man to take something as his god without proof or evidence. Al-Saadi: 262.\nWhat is the reason for Abraham (peace be upon him) to call a star as his lord?\nفَلَمَّآ أَفَلَ قَالَ لَآ أُحِبُّ ٱلۡأٓفِلِينَ ٧٦\nMeaning: That which disappears from the sight of its worshiper, as the object of worship should take care of its worshiper, and should manage all of his affairs. As for what disappears for a long time, how can it deserve to be worshiped? Is taking it as a god anything but the utmost foolishness and the worst falsehood? Al-Saadi: 262.\nThat which disappears from its worshipers does not deserve to be worshiped. Why?\nقَالَ لَئِن لَّمۡ يَهۡدِنِي رَبِّي لَأَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلضَّآلِّينَ ٧٧\nThe Prophets (peace be upon them) ask Allah constantly to keep them steadfast in their faith, as Abraham (peace be upon him) said: (and keep me and my sons away from worshipping idols) [14:35]. Al-Baghawi: 2/41.\nGive an example of the Prophets (peace be upon them) concern for being steadfast in their faith?\nإِنِّي وَجَّهۡتُ وَجۡهِيَ لِلَّذِي فَطَرَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ حَنِيفٗاۖ وَمَآ أَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ٧٩\nMeaning: I have directed my worship toward the One Who created heavens and earth, the Everlasting, the Giver of life and Bringer of death, not to a mortal and useless idols. Al-Tabari: 11/487.\nWhat are the reasons for worshiping Allah and not something else?\nوَكَيۡفَ أَخَافُ مَآ أَشۡرَكۡتُمۡ وَلَا تَخَافُونَ أَنَّكُمۡ أَشۡرَكۡتُم بِٱللَّهِ مَا لَمۡ يُنَزِّلۡ بِهِۦ عَلَيۡكُمۡ سُلۡطَٰنٗاۚ فَأَيُّ ٱلۡفَرِيقَيۡنِ أَحَقُّ بِٱلۡأَمۡنِۖ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٨١ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَلَمۡ يَلۡبِسُوٓاْ إِيمَٰنَهُم بِظُلۡمٍ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمُ ٱلۡأَمۡنُ وَهُم مُّهۡتَدُونَ ٨٢\nMeaning: How can I fear inanimate objects while you do not fear Allah, the All-Mighty. (So which of the two parties has more right to feel secure) from the punishment of Allah, the believer or the polytheist? Allah answers, (They who believe and do not mix their belief with injustice), which is shirk. Al-Qurtubi: 8/444.\nFearing inanimate objects more than Allah is a total ignorance. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nجَنَّGrew dark\nالآفِلِينَThose that set\nأَفَلَSet\nحَنِيفًاInclining toward truth"],[138,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nRead with reflection the interpretation of this verse and draw three useful lessons.\nIdentify three religious matters of which you have difficulty understanding, then contact a scholar to ask him about them. Let that be your approach to all ambiguous matters. Your rank in this life and in the Hereafter increases with your knowledge.\nIdentify three traits of the Prophets (peace be upon them) and follow their example.\nguid\nAttaining the sincere belief in the Oneness of Allah grants you security from all fears in this life and in the Hereafter.\nBeing guided to the straight path is the best thing a person can have in this life.\nIf the Prophets committed any act of shirk (associating others with Allah), all of their good deeds will be nullified, so imagine how it would be for those who are below them.\nrefl\nوَتِلۡكَ حُجَّتُنَآ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهَآ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ عَلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦۚ نَرۡفَعُ دَرَجَٰتٖ مَّن نَّشَآءُۗ\nMeaning: We have rewarded Abraham (peace be upon him) for his obedience, sincerity in believing in the Oneness of his Lord, and migrating from his people who were disbelievers - by elevating him in ranks, giving him his reward in this life and giving to him children who were selected as Prophets with honored descendants who were preferred over the rest of the people [of their times]. Al-Tabari: 11/507.\nWhoever gives up something for the sake of Allah, Allah will give him something much better instead. Explain in light of this verse\nوَتِلۡكَ حُجَّتُنَآ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهَآ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ عَلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦۚ نَرۡفَعُ دَرَجَٰتٖ مَّن نَّشَآءُۗ\nAllah elevates one who has knowledge above other people in ranks, especially the scholar who acts upon his knowledge and teaches others; Allah makes him a leader for the people to follow, according to his situation, whereby his deeds are watched, his footsteps followed, and his light is sought so that people may walk in the light of his knowledge. Al-Saadi: 263.\nWhat is the reason for elevating Abraham (peace be upon him) in ranks over his people?\nنَرۡفَعُ دَرَجَٰتٖ مَّن نَّشَآءُۗ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ حَكِيمٌ عَلِيمٞ ٨٣\nMeaning: We elevate in ranks whom We will with knowledge, understanding, virtue and wisdom, as We did for Abraham when he became guided, and debated his people over the Oneness of Allah. Al-Baghawi: 2/41.\nHow does the believer become elevated in ranks?\nوَوَهَبۡنَا لَهُۥٓ إِسۡحَٰقَ وَيَعۡقُوبَۚ كُلًّا هَدَيۡنَاۚ وَنُوحًا هَدَيۡنَا مِن قَبۡلُۖ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِهِۦ دَاوُۥدَ وَسُلَيۡمَٰنَ وَأَيُّوبَ وَيُوسُفَ وَمُوسَىٰ وَهَٰرُونَۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٨٤\nThis was a reward for Abraham (peace be upon him), who left his people and migrated from their land, so that he could worship Allah alone. Allah compensated Abraham (peace be upon him) for leaving his people and tribe when He gave him righteous children of his own, who would follow his religion so that his eyes would be comforted by them. Ibn Kathir: 2/147.\nThe children were a reward for the righteousness of Abraham (peace be upon him). How?\nوَلَوۡ أَشۡرَكُواْ لَحَبِطَ عَنۡهُم مَّا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٨٨\n(And if they were to associate others with Him), hypothetically speaking, (all their deeds would have been nullified) for ascribing partners to Allah invalidates all good deeds and incurs eternity in Hellfire. If these chosen elite had ascribed partners to Allah -which is unlikely as they are far above doing such a thing- all their good deeds would come to nothing, and this result would apply even more to others. Al-Saadi: 264.\nAscribing partners to Allah, even by righteous people, invalidates all good deeds. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَوۡ أَشۡرَكُواْ لَحَبِطَ عَنۡهُم مَّا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٨٨\nMeaning: If they worshiped other than Me, I would have nullified their deeds, however, I protected them from shirk. Al-Qurtubi: 8/451.\nWhat is the punishment for associating others with Allah while having good deeds?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ هَدَى ٱللَّهُۖ فَبِهُدَىٰهُمُ ٱقۡتَدِهۡۗ\nMeaning: Follow -O noble Messenger- in the footsteps of these chosen Prophets, and tread their path. The Prophet (ﷺ) complied with this command, and followed the guidance of the Messengers who came before him; he acquired all perfect attributes and virtues by means of which he surpassed all people, and was the leader of the Messengers, foremost among the pious -may the blessings and peace of Allah be upon him and upon all of them. Al-Saadi: 264.\nThis verse indicates that the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) takes precedence over all other Messengers. How?\nwords\nيَلبِسُواThey mix\nوَاجتَبَينَاهُمWe chose them\nاقتَدِهFollow"],[139,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nRemind yourself of three blessings of the Quran upon you or upon the Muslim nation.\nGo to prayer early today, and fulfill its pillars and conditions as Allah commands.\nReckon with yourself by contrasting your major sins with your good deeds that you had in the past, and remind yourself of the Day of Judgement.\nguid\nReflect on the forbearance of Allah where He hears annoyances from people and their rejection of His Messengers, but He does not hasten to punish them so that they may believe and revert to Him.\nBond to the Quran through recitation and reflection to receive its blessings.\nEverything you accumulate in this life will perish and fade away, then you will stand alone before Allah.\nrefl\nوَمَا قَدَرُواْ ٱللَّهَ حَقَّ قَدۡرِهِۦٓ إِذۡ قَالُواْ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ بَشَرٖ مِّن شَيۡءٖۗ قُلۡ مَنۡ أَنزَلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ ٱلَّذِي جَآءَ بِهِۦ مُوسَىٰ\nAnd they have not revered Allah His true reverence), they did not have true knowledge of Him, His Graciousness and Mercy to His servants since they denied the fact that He sent Messengers and revealed Scriptures. The Jews were the ones who made that claim considering the subsequent response from Allah. They said that in exaggerated denial of the Prophethood of Muhammad (ﷺ). Ibn Juzay: 1/278.\nWhat is the sign of revering Allah His true reverence?\nوَمَا قَدَرُواْ ٱللَّهَ حَقَّ قَدۡرِهِۦٓ\nIbn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \"The meaning of this verse applies to the disbelievers only, since whoever believes that Allah is Most Capable of all things, then he revered Allah His true reverence.\" Ibn Taimyah: 3/53.\nWho revers Allah His true reverence?\nوَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّنِ ٱفۡتَرَىٰ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبًا أَوۡ قَالَ أُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ وَلَمۡ يُوحَ إِلَيۡهِ شَيۡءٞ\nAmong this type of wrongdoers is one who turned away from the Prophet's Sunnah and the way of the righteous predecessors. So, he would say: I have a hunch about this matter, or my heart tells me this about such matter. And so, they rule by how they feel in their hearts and by whatever thoughts that come to them. They set aside the rules of Sharia, saying: These rules are meant for the fools and general public, but the elite allies do not need them. Al-Qurtubi: 8/458.\nWhen thoughts of the heart and dreams are considered a source of rules of Sharia, does that constitute fabricating lies against Allah?\nوَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّنِ ٱفۡتَرَىٰ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبًا أَوۡ قَالَ أُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ وَلَمۡ يُوحَ إِلَيۡهِ شَيۡءٞ وَمَن قَالَ سَأُنزِلُ مِثۡلَ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُۗ\nNo one does more wrong or greater evil than the one who tells lies against Allah, by attributing to Him words or rulings that have nothing to do with Him. Indeed, this is the worst of characteristics, because it involves lying and changing religious teachings in both the fundamental and minor issues, and attributing that to Allah. This is one of the worst of evil deeds. Al-Saadi: 265.\nNo one does greater wrong than one who fabricates lies against Allah. Why?\nوَلَوۡ تَرَىٰٓ إِذِ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ فِي غَمَرَٰتِ ٱلۡمَوۡتِ وَٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ بَاسِطُوٓاْ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ أَخۡرِجُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمُۖ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ تُجۡزَوۡنَ عَذَابَ ٱلۡهُونِ بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَقُولُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ غَيۡرَ ٱلۡحَقِّ وَكُنتُمۡ عَنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ تَسۡتَكۡبِرُونَ ٩٣\n(While the angels are stretching out their hands) tormenting them and striking their faces and their backs, moreover, it is said: Tormenting them by taking their souls. The angels say, (Give up your souls) unwillingly, because the believer' soul is elated for meeting its Lord while the disbeliever' soul hates that. It means that if only you could see that, you would be astonished. Al-Baghawi: 2/47.\nWhat is the difference between the believer and disbeliever at the time of death?\nوَلَقَدۡ جِئۡتُمُونَا فُرَٰدَىٰ كَمَا خَلَقۡنَٰكُمۡ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٖ وَتَرَكۡتُم مَّا خَوَّلۡنَٰكُمۡ وَرَآءَ ظُهُورِكُمۡۖ\nMeaning: You have come to Us one by one, each one is alone without his family, wealth, children or helper from those who accompanied him before in his wrongdoing. Al-Qurtubi: 8/461.\nOne's wealth, family and children are all considered adornment of the worldly life. Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ جِئۡتُمُونَا فُرَٰدَىٰ كَمَا خَلَقۡنَٰكُمۡ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٖ وَتَرَكۡتُم مَّا خَوَّلۡنَٰكُمۡ وَرَآءَ ظُهُورِكُمۡۖ وَمَا نَرَىٰ مَعَكُمۡ شُفَعَآءَكُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ زَعَمۡتُمۡ أَنَّهُمۡ فِيكُمۡ شُرَكَٰٓؤُاْۚ\nAll creatures are servants of Allah, and Allah is their Sovereign and the only One Who is deserving of their worship. On the Day of Resurrection, they will be rebuked for associating others in worship with Allah and devoting worship to some of His servants, ascribing to them the status of the Creator and Sovereign. Al-Saadi: 265.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, those who worship righteous men will have great remorse. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nغَمَرَاتِAgonies\nخَوَّلنَاكُمWe bestowed on you\nتَقَطَّعَ بَينَكُمSevered bonds between you"],[140,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nThink of an example where Allah brought a living out of the dead, and a dead out of the living, and reflect upon His Power.\nLearn the importance of the lunar calendar for defining the times for acts of worship, and strive to memorize the lunar months so that you do not miss out on good deeds.\nSleep early tonight, as that is the natural order of things and it is also a Sunnah.\nguid\nWhoever approaches the Quran with an open mind and heart, is worthy of understanding the meanings of the verses, as opposed to the one who has a closed mind and heart.\nIt is worth reflecting upon Allah's creation of the food we eat, and how it differs in taste and texture.\nIf you hear someone fabricating lies against Allah, then glorify Allah and exalt Him above what the unjust atheists are saying.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ فَالِقُ ٱلۡحَبِّ وَٱلنَّوَىٰۖ يُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡحَيَّ مِنَ ٱلۡمَيِّتِ وَمُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡمَيِّتِ مِنَ ٱلۡحَيِّۚ ذَٰلِكُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ فَأَنَّىٰ تُؤۡفَكُونَ ٩٥\nAllah mentions many wonders of His making that the idols of disbelievers are helpless to make the smallest of them. Al-Qurtubi: 8/465.\nWhat is the wisdom behind mentioning the wonders of Allah's creation in this verse?\nيُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡحَيَّ مِنَ ٱلۡمَيِّتِ وَمُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡمَيِّتِ مِنَ ٱلۡحَيِّۚ ذَٰلِكُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ فَأَنَّىٰ تُؤۡفَكُونَ ٩٥ فَالِقُ ٱلۡإِصۡبَاحِ وَجَعَلَ ٱلَّيۡلَ سَكَنٗا وَٱلشَّمۡسَ وَٱلۡقَمَرَ حُسۡبَانٗاۚ\nAllah reminds of His ability to create diversified and contrasting things which testify to His perfect greatness and supreme power. Ibn Kathir: 2/150.\nAllah is able of creating diversified and contrasting things. What does that indicate?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلنُّجُومَ لِتَهۡتَدُواْ بِهَا فِي ظُلُمَٰتِ ٱلۡبَرِّ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِۗ قَدۡ فَصَّلۡنَا ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٩٧\nThis verse and similar verses indicate that it is permitted to learn about the movement and positions of the stars, a science that is called astronomy, as navigation is not possible without it. Al-Saadi: 266.\nWhat is lawful and the unlawful about learning the movement of the stars?\nقَدۡ فَصَّلۡنَا ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٩٨\nMeaning: For people of knowledge, as they are the ones who are addressed here and from whom a response is required; unlike the ignorant and harsh people who turn away from the signs of Allah, and from the knowledge brought by the Messengers, as detailing will be of no benefit to them, an explanation will not dispel their confusion, and clarification will not resolve their uncertainty. Al-Saadi: 266.\nThe people of knowledge were selected to be addressed with detailing of the signs. Why?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّخۡلِ مِن طَلۡعِهَا قِنۡوَانٞ دَانِيَةٞ\nThe clusters of dates hanging low are mentioned to show the power and grace of Allah, and for people to be grateful for the proximity of its fruit. Al-Qurtubi: 8/472.\nWhy are the clusters of dates hanging low selected for mention in this verse?\nٱنظُرُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ ثَمَرِهِۦٓ إِذَآ أَثۡمَرَ وَيَنۡعِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكُمۡ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٩٩\nTake a look with contemplation, not an empty glance. Al-Qurtubi: 8/472.\nWhat is the commanded look in this verse?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكُمۡ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٩٩\nThe faith of the believers makes them strive in accordance with its requirements and demands, part of which is to contemplate the signs of Allah and learn from them the intended lessons, and what they guide to, as validated by sound reason, common sense and Islamic teachings. Al-Saadi: 267.\nWhy are the believers selected to benefit from the signs of Allah?\nwords\nتُؤفَكُونَYou become deluded\nقِنوَانٌ دَانِيَةٌClusters of dates hanging low\nوَيَنعِهِIts ripening\nوَخَرَقُواThey have fabricated for Him"],[141,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nSearch for verses in the Quran about an issue that concerns you and read their interpretation and ask about their meanings.\nSay: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with you from my evil deed becoming appealing to me.\"\nSay: \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\"\nguid\nUphold the revelations (The Holy Quran and Sunnah), and do not substitute them for anything.\nDo not act in a way that repels your opponent from following the rightful way of the Quran and Sunnah. Use wisdom, for it is the greatest tool when inviting others to the path of Allah.\nTurning away from the truth is punished by turning one's heart away from guidance and truth for good, so beware of that.\nrefl\nذَٰلِكُمُ ٱللَّهُ رَبُّكُمۡۖ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَۖ خَٰلِقُ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ فَٱعۡبُدُوهُۚ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ وَكِيلٞ ١٠٢\n(That is Allah, your Lord), He is the only One to be worshipped, the only One Who is deserving of the utmost humility and love, the Lord Who nourishes all of His creations with His blessings and wards off all kinds of calamities. Al-Saadi: 268.\nWhat is the meaning of the word (Lord)? What does its meaning entail?\nوَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ وَكِيلٞ ١٠٢\nWhen people are being in charge of things, they are in charge on behalf of someone else, and the proxy receives instructions from the one who put him in charge. But when we speak of Allah being in charge, He is in charge by and for Himself, which is indicative of His perfect knowledge, proper running of affairs, excellence and justice. It is not possible for anyone to check on Him, or find flaws or problems in His creation or find any faults or shortcomings in the way in which He governs all affairs. Al-Saadi: 268.\nWhat is the difference between people being in charge and Allah being in charge?\nلَّا تُدۡرِكُهُ ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرُ وَهُوَ يُدۡرِكُ ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرَۖ وَهُوَ ٱللَّطِيفُ ٱلۡخَبِيرُ ١٠٣\nThe verse negates encompassing but does not negate the sighting since only nullity cannot be seen and that is not a praiseworthy. The real praiseworthy is in the fact that Allah can be seen but can not be encompassed, and this is similar to being known but can not be fully comprehended. Ibn Taimyah: 3/78-79.\nHow can we infer from this verse the sighting of Allah by the believers on the Last Day?\nٱتَّبِعۡ مَآ أُوحِيَ إِلَيۡكَ مِن رَّبِّكَۖ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَۖ وَأَعۡرِضۡ عَنِ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١٠٦\nMeaning: Do not occupy yourself with them, rather engage yourself with worshiping Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 8/490.\nWhat should you engage yourself with in this life?\nوَلَا تَسُبُّواْ ٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ فَيَسُبُّواْ ٱللَّهَ عَدۡوَۢا بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖۗ\nAllah forbids the believers from insulting the idols of disbelievers since that would turn them away and increase them in their disbelief. Al-Qurtubi: 8/491.\nAllah forbids the believers from insulting the idols of disbelievers. Why?\nوَلَا تَسُبُّواْ ٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ فَيَسُبُّواْ ٱللَّهَ عَدۡوَۢا بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖۗ\nThis verse points to an important Sharia principle, which is: Means are to be judged by ends, and means that may lead to something prohibited - even if those means are permissible - are to be deemed prohibited also, if they will lead to evil. Al-Saadi: 269.\nScholars deduced an important principle from this verse. What is it?\nوَلَا تَسُبُّواْ ٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ فَيَسُبُّواْ ٱللَّهَ عَدۡوَۢا بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖۗ\nWhen the disbelievers are in power and feared that they may revile Islam, the Prophet (ﷺ) or Allah, then it is forbidden for a Muslim to revile their religion, crosses or anything that may lead to that. Ibn Atiyah:2/332.\nWhen is it wise not to revile the gods of the disbelievers?\nwords\nنُصَرِّفُWe explain\nدَرَستَYou have studied\nعَدوًاIn enmity\nيَعمَهُونَThey are bewildered"],[142,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah often for guidance and to make you firm upon Islam, as guidance is only in His Hand.\nRead a book about global Zionists' plans in order to understand the perspective of the devils among mankind who are the enemies of the Prophets (peace be upon them).\nLearn more from a lecture or reading a book about Sharia rulings on animal sacrifices to know which are permissible to eat and which are prohibited.\nguid\nOne of the methods used by people of falsehood is uttering elegant words of deception while their speech inherently leads only to corruption.\nThe hearts that lack belief in Allah are the hearts that incline the most toward people of desires and suspicions .\nAbundance is not evidence of truth.\nrefl\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلۡنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِيٍّ عَدُوّٗا شَيَٰطِينَ ٱلۡإِنسِ وَٱلۡجِنِّ يُوحِي بَعۡضُهُمۡ إِلَىٰ بَعۡضٖ زُخۡرُفَ ٱلۡقَوۡلِ غُرُورٗاۚ\nQatadah, Mujahid and Alhasan said: \"There are devils among mankind, as there are among jinn.\" Malik bin Dinar said: \"The devils from mankind are more dangerous to me than those from the jinn because I can rid of the latter by seeking refuge with Allah, but the former comes visibly and pulls me into committing sins.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/56.\nAre there devils among mankind as there are among jinn? Which are more dangerous?\nيُوحِي بَعۡضُهُمۡ إِلَىٰ بَعۡضٖ زُخۡرُفَ ٱلۡقَوۡلِ غُرُورٗاۚ\nMeaning: They make fair-seeming to one another the falsehood to which they call people, and they come up with flowery words and depict it in the best image, so as to deceive the foolish who do not understand the reality of things. Thus, the foolish are deceived by these fancy words and flowery phrases, so they believe truth to be falsehood and falsehood to be true. Al-Saadi: 269-270.\nWhy do the people of falsehood use fancy words and flowery phrases?\nوَلِتَصۡغَىٰٓ إِلَيۡهِ أَفۡـِٔدَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ وَلِيَرۡضَوۡهُ\nAllah states that those who disbelieve in the Hereafter will incline toward the words of enemies of Messengers. Thus, disobeying the Messengers and disbelief in the Hereafter are correlated. Whoever does not believe in the Hereafter, will incline toward the deception of enemies of the Messengers as it is the case with many disbelievers and hypocrites in this nation and in others. Ibn Taimyah: 3/89-90.\nDisobeying the Messengers and disbelieving in the Hereafter are correlated. Explain.\nوَتَمَّتۡ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ صِدۡقٗا وَعَدۡلٗاۚ لَّا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمَٰتِهِۦۚ وَهُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ١١٥\n(And the word of your Lord has been fulfilled in truth and in justice), Allah sent His Messengers with Knowledge and justice; therefore, the greater one's attainment of knowledge and justice, the closer he will be to what the Messengers were sent with. Ibn Taimyah: 3/93.\nWhat are the things that determine your closeness to what the Messengers (p) were sent with?\nوَإِن تُطِعۡ أَكۡثَرَ مَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ يُضِلُّوكَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ إِن يَتَّبِعُونَ إِلَّا ٱلظَّنَّ وَإِنۡ هُمۡ إِلَّا يَخۡرُصُونَ ١١٦\nThe reason that misguided people are a majority is the fact that truth and guidance require sound minds, virtuous souls, reflection on what is good and bad, giving precedence to truth over whim, rationality over desire and wishing the best to all people. If any of these traits is repressed, then misguidance would infiltrate the soul commensurate with the extent of that repression. Ibn Ashur: 8/25.\nThe majority of people on earth are misguided. Why?\nوَإِن تُطِعۡ أَكۡثَرَ مَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ يُضِلُّوكَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ١١٦\nThis verse indicates that neither truth is determined by abundancy of followers, nor falsehood is determined by scarcity of followers. Rather, the reality is something other than that, for the people of truth are the fewest in number, but are the greatest in esteem and reward before Allah. Al-Saadi: 270.\nIt is common, nowadays, for one to believe views of the majority rather than that of the minority. What is the rule of Sharia on this matter?\nفَكُلُواْ مِمَّا ذُكِرَ ٱسۡمُ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡهِ إِن كُنتُم بِـَٔايَٰتِهِۦ مُؤۡمِنِينَ ١١٨\n(If you are believers in His verses) this means that you will abide if you follow Allah's commands and rules, since believing in the rules of Allah necessitates adhering and following them. Ibn Atiyah:2/338.\nAfter commanding to eat that upon which the name of Allah has been mentioned, the verse is concluded with mentioning the belief in Allah's verses. Why?\nwords\nقُبُلًاFace to face\nغُرُورًاDelusion\nوَلِتَصغَىWill incline toward\nوَلِيَقتَرِفُواThey will commit\nيَخرُصُونَMisjudging and lying"],[143,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nMention Allah's name before eating.\nReckon with yourself today for the concealed sins you may commit that is apparent to none but Allah.\nShare a message in which you advise others not to eat anything over which Allah's name is not mentioned.\nguid\nIt is obligatory to desist sins whether they are hidden or apparent, and whether they are deeds of the heart or actions of the body.\nEnsure that you consume only lawful food such as slaughtered meat over which the name of Allah is mentioned.\nPolytheism is death (of the soul) and darkness while faith in Allah is life and light.\nrefl\nوَقَدۡ فَصَّلَ لَكُم مَّا حَرَّمَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ\nThis verse indicates that the basic rule on things and food is that they are permissible, and that if there is no Sharia text to indicate that a thing is prohibited, then it remains permissible. Whatever Allah has remained silent about is permissible, because Allah has detailed that which is prohibited. If He has not clearly declared it to be prohibited, then it is not prohibited. Al-Saadi: 271.\nHow do we infer from this verse this basic rule: All things remain permissible except what is declared to be prohibited ?\nوَإِنَّ كَثِيرٗا لَّيُضِلُّونَ بِأَهۡوَآئِهِم بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٍۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ أَعۡلَمُ بِٱلۡمُعۡتَدِينَ ١١٩\nThis applies to anyone who follows a passion or an ecstasy without guidance from Allah, whether it is out of love or hatred. One must not follow whatever he loves as a religious act nor calls others to it. Moreover, when one does not like something, he must not take this hatred as a religious act and forbids others from it, unless it is led by Allah's guidance which is His Sharia (divine law) that He ordained to His Messenger (ﷺ). Therefore, whoever follows his whim out of love or hatred for something without guidance from Sharia, then he is following his desire without guidance from Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 3/96.\nExplain the risk of following one's own whims without Allah's guidance?\nوَإِنَّ كَثِيرٗا لَّيُضِلُّونَ بِأَهۡوَآئِهِم بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٍۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ أَعۡلَمُ بِٱلۡمُعۡتَدِينَ ١١٩\nAllah Has made clear that their misguidance is the worst of its kind since it is driven by whims and not by reason and reflection. (Without any knowledge), which means without reason. Ibn Atiyah:2/339.\nWhat is the worst kind of misguidance?\nوَذَرُواْ ظَٰهِرَ ٱلۡإِثۡمِ وَبَاطِنَهُۥٓۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَكۡسِبُونَ ٱلۡإِثۡمَ سَيُجۡزَوۡنَ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَقۡتَرِفُونَ ١٢٠\nThe individual does not fully give up sin, either outward or hidden, until he learns what it is and finds out about it. Finding out about it and learning what constitutes sin, both outward or hidden, so that one is aware of it, is an individual obligation for everyone who is accountable. Many people are unaware of many sins, especially the sins of the heart such as arrogance, self-admiration, showing off and so on, to such an extent that a person may commit many of these sins without being aware of them, because of lack of knowledge and understanding. Al-Saadi: 271.\nFor an individual, what is first thing to do to avoid committing outward and hidden sins?\nوَذَرُواْ ظَٰهِرَ ٱلۡإِثۡمِ وَبَاطِنَهُۥٓۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَكۡسِبُونَ ٱلۡإِثۡمَ سَيُجۡزَوۡنَ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَقۡتَرِفُونَ ١٢٠\n(And avoid committing sin, whether openly or in secret), this includes all sins since they are all committed either openly or in secret. It is said that (openly) refers to sinful actions while (in secret) refers to sinful beliefs. Ibn Juzay: 1/284.\nThis verse employs a concise style to convey general meanings. Explain.\nوَإِنَّ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينَ لَيُوحُونَ إِلَىٰٓ أَوۡلِيَآئِهِمۡ لِيُجَٰدِلُوكُمۡۖ\nThis verse indicates that inspirations and spiritual revelations, a phenomenon that is particularly spread among Sufis and their ilk, is not to be regarded as truth on its own, and should not be accepted until it has been checked against the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger (ﷺ). If the Quran and Sunnah testify in its favor, then it may be accepted, but if it is contrary to them, then it is to be rejected. If the evidence is absent, then judgement is to be reserved and it is to be neither accepted nor rejected because revelation and inspiration may come from the Most Merciful, or it may come from the devil, so it is essential to distinguish between the two and to see the difference between them. Failing to see the difference between them leads to errors and misguidance the extent of which can only be known by Allah. Al-Saadi: 271.\nUsing this verse, how do you respond to one who accepts inspirations and spiritual revelations without having them checked against the Quran and Sunnah?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلۡنَا فِي كُلِّ قَرۡيَةٍ أَكَٰبِرَ مُجۡرِمِيهَا لِيَمۡكُرُواْ فِيهَاۖ وَمَا يَمۡكُرُونَ إِلَّا بِأَنفُسِهِمۡ وَمَا يَشۡعُرُونَ ١٢٣\n(Thus We have placed in every city the greatest), just like we placed in Makkah its greatest criminals, we had done the same in every city. The greatest criminals were mentioned because the rest of the criminals follow them. Ibn Juzay: 1/284.\nThe verse mentions only the greatest criminals. Why?\nwords\nصَغَارٌDisgrace"],[144,"§Al-An'am\ndeeds\nPray to Allah that He opens your heart to the truth wherever it is.\nRemind yourself of Allah's blessing of guidance that was bestowed upon you when He opened your heart to Islam, and that had He willed otherwise, you would not have been guided.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the evil of the jinn.\nguid\nGuidance is from Allah, hence ask Him for guidance.\nThe disbelieving hearts reside within them all that is evil from desires and doubts, and are hotbeds for the devil .\nIncrease your good deeds, as they lead you to be an ally of Allah.\nrefl\nفَمَن يُرِدِ ٱللَّهُ أَن يَهۡدِيَهُۥ يَشۡرَحۡ صَدۡرَهُۥ لِلۡإِسۡلَٰمِۖ\nAllah describes to His servants the sign of a person who is blessed and guided. If Allah opens a person's heart to Islam, and it is filled with the light of faith and certainty, so that he feels at ease with it, loves good deeds and finds joy in doing them, and does not find them burdensome, then this is a sign that Allah has guided him and has blessed him with faith and led him to the straight path. Al-Saadi: 272.\nWhat is the sign of guidance that one feels within himself?\nوَمَن يُرِدۡ أَن يُضِلَّهُۥ يَجۡعَلۡ صَدۡرَهُۥ ضَيِّقًا حَرَجٗا كَأَنَّمَا يَصَّعَّدُ فِي ٱلسَّمَآءِۚ\nFor one who is gone astray, accepting faith is as hard as trying to climb up into the sky, which is not possible. Ibn Juzay: 1/285.\nWhat is the similarity between one who is gone astray and another who wants to climb up into the sky?\nوَمَن يُرِدۡ أَن يُضِلَّهُۥ يَجۡعَلۡ صَدۡرَهُۥ ضَيِّقًا حَرَجٗا كَأَنَّمَا يَصَّعَّدُ فِي ٱلسَّمَآءِۚ\nAllah Has compared the disbeliever's repulsion toward faith to one who overburdened himself with what he could not bear just as climbing up into the sky is not bearable. Al-Qurtubi: 9/25.\nFor one who is gone astray, accepting faith is difficult or rather impossible. Explain.\nلَهُمۡ دَارُ ٱلسَّلَٰمِ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡۖ وَهُوَ وَلِيُّهُم بِمَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ١٢٧\nHome of Peace is Paradise in the Hereafter. It is called that because everyone who enters it is safe from all tribulations and calamities. Al-Baghawi: 2/63.\nWhat is (Home of Peace)? Why is it called that?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ نُوَلِّي بَعۡضَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ بَعۡضَۢا بِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ١٢٩\nMeaning: It is Our way to create an alliance between every wrongdoer and another one like him to entice him and urge him to do evil, and to turn him away and divert him from goodness. This is a severe punishment from Allah, with terrible consequences and a serious impact. It is the wrongdoer's fault, because he is the one who brought it upon himself. (And your Lord is never unjust to His slaves) [41:46]. If people do a great deal of corruption and evil, and they withhold what is due from them, Allah will put evildoers in charge of them, who will afflict them with the worst torment, and will take from them unjustly and by force many times more than what they withheld of what is due to Allah and to His servants. Al-Saadi: 273.\nDescribe two examples of the alliance between wrongdoers.\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ نُوَلِّي بَعۡضَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ بَعۡضَۢا بِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ١٢٩\nThis is a threat to the wrongdoer that if he does not cease his transgression, Allah will empower another wrongdoer over him. Fudhail bin Iyadh said: \"When you see a wrongdoer taking revenge on another, pause and reflect with wonder.\" Al-Qurtubi: 9/30.\nHow does Allah punish a wrongdoer in this life?\nيَٰمَعۡشَرَ ٱلۡجِنِّ وَٱلۡإِنسِ أَلَمۡ يَأۡتِكُمۡ رُسُلٞ مِّنكُمۡ يَقُصُّونَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ ءَايَٰتِي وَيُنذِرُونَكُمۡ لِقَآءَ يَوۡمِكُمۡ هَٰذَاۚ قَالُواْ شَهِدۡنَا عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِنَاۖ وَغَرَّتۡهُمُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَشَهِدُواْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ أَنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ كَٰفِرِينَ ١٣٠\nMeaning: Messengers from among you had come with clear proofs alerting you to the wrongs that you have been doing, and warning you of Allah's punishment, but you did not accept nor remember nor reflect. Al-Tabari: 12/120.\nAlerting the wrongdoers to their transgression before punishment is the approach of the Quran. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nحَرَجًاConstricted\nيَصَّعَّدُ فِي السَّمَاءِClimbing up into the sky\nالرِّجسَDefilement\nدَارُ السَّلاَمِHome of Peace\nاستَمتَعَBenefited"]])